Moduledrum's third patch for dsp56300 (sd88me's fork at 26558e5401fa134a013eca8dbb8c5ecde837ec55, ext/dsp56300): MSVC
portability, not emulation (.clew increment 0021, the Windows build). It changes no instruction's behaviour. The change is
marked "MD patch" in the source. 0001 (JIT fixes) and 0002 (memory) are independent of it (different files); any order applies.

1. dsp56kEmu/dsp.h, DSP::callInstruction and DSP::getRecompInfo: the fork's arm32 static-recompiler helpers rebuild a
   TInstructionFunc (a pointer to a DSP member function) from a raw address by copying a {ptr, adjustment} pair into it, and
   asserted that the member pointer is two pointers wide, the Itanium C++ ABI's layout. MSVC's member pointer to a class
   without bases is one pointer, so the static_assert stopped every file that includes dsp.h (dsp.h(358): error C2338).
   Now the copy is sizeof(member pointer) bytes from {ptr, 0}, which is the right value on both ABIs, and the assertion only
   rules out anything wider than the pair. The helpers are not used by Moduledrum (the static recompiler is the MPC port's);
   the fix keeps them compiling everywhere.

diff --git a/source/dsp56kEmu/dsp.h b/source/dsp56kEmu/dsp.h
index 4d8f44de..e8365d0c 100644
--- a/source/dsp56kEmu/dsp.h
+++ b/source/dsp56kEmu/dsp.h
@@ -355,7 +355,9 @@ namespace dsp56k
 		void callInstruction(void* _rawFunc, TWord _op) noexcept
 		{
 			TInstructionFunc f;
-			static_assert(sizeof(f) == 2 * sizeof(void*), "expected the Itanium member-pointer layout {ptr, adjustment}");
+			// MD patch: a member pointer is {ptr, adjustment} on the Itanium C++ ABI and a single pointer on MSVC (DSP has
+			// no bases); copying sizeof(f) from {ptr, 0} builds the right value on both
+			static_assert(sizeof(f) <= 2 * sizeof(void*), "expected a member pointer of at most {ptr, adjustment}");
 			void* raw[2] = { _rawFunc, nullptr };
 			std::memcpy(&f, raw, sizeof(f));
 			exec_jump(f, _op);
@@ -390,7 +392,7 @@ namespace dsp56k
 		RecompInfo getRecompInfo(TWord _pc) const noexcept
 		{
 			const auto& e = m_opcodeCache[_pc];
-			auto raw = [](const TInstructionFunc& _f) { void* r[2]; std::memcpy(r, &_f, sizeof(r)); return r[0]; };
+			auto raw = [](const TInstructionFunc& _f) { void* r[2] = { nullptr, nullptr }; std::memcpy(r, &_f, sizeof(_f)); return r[0]; };   // MD patch: sizeof(_f), see callInstruction
 			return { raw(e.op), raw(e.opMove), raw(e.opAlu), e.op == &DSP::op_Parallel, e.op != &DSP::op_ResolveCache };
 		}
 		bool runRecompiled(TWord _pc) noexcept;
